00:28:50.500 --> 00:28:51.820
You're going to see that a lot now.

631
00:28:52.040 --> 00:28:55.360
Now that you've spotted it once, it's going to be something you can never unsee.

632
00:28:55.640 --> 00:28:57.500
All right, guys, we have something new to track.

633
00:28:57.680 --> 00:29:00.000
Who's drinking coffee in conference room scenes?

634
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:07.960
Well, one of my favorite moments in this conference room scene, Angela, is Mindy's line when she says, I have a lot of questions.

635
00:29:08.180 --> 00:29:09.280
Number one, how dare you?

636
00:29:09.880 --> 00:29:11.600
I loved it so much.

637
00:29:11.600 --> 00:29:17.760
We got a fan question from Jocelyn Sumi, who said, this is the line that is most quoted by my family.

638
00:29:17.760 --> 00:29:19.720
So I have to know who wrote it.

639
00:29:19.980 --> 00:29:21.800
Please tell me it was Mindy Kaling.

640
00:29:22.400 --> 00:29:22.840
Yes.

641
00:29:23.140 --> 00:29:28.560
Mindy wrote this line and she was asked about this line in an interview she did with Office Tally.

642
00:29:28.740 --> 00:29:29.820
And I loved her answer.

643
00:29:30.040 --> 00:29:30.940
Oh, let's hear it.

644
00:29:31.060 --> 00:29:32.060
Here's what she said.

645
00:29:32.060 --> 00:29:36.260
Quote, I never intentionally give myself the funniest lines.

646
00:29:36.460 --> 00:29:41.700
However, they often resonate as the funniest because of my gifts as a comic actor.

647
00:29:42.500 --> 00:29:47.480
Sometimes I try to give myself really drab, unfunny lines so as to not steal focus.

648
00:29:47.480 --> 00:29:51.380
But even that doesn't work because they always sparkle upon delivery.

649
00:29:51.580 --> 00:29:52.400
It's hard.

650
00:29:53.700 --> 00:29:55.560
It's hard being so fabulous, y'all.

651
00:29:55.880 --> 00:29:57.000
But I just loved that.

652
00:29:57.080 --> 00:29:58.020
I thought it was really funny.

653
00:29:58.240 --> 00:29:59.260
That is really funny.

654
00:29:59.540 --> 00:30:02.720
I had a friend when I lived in New York in my 20s.

655
00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:06.900
And whenever she'd get a little tipsy, inevitably, she'd say, how dare you?

656
00:30:08.020 --> 00:30:10.500
Like we'd be like, hey, listen, we got to go.

657
00:30:10.680 --> 00:30:11.700
Let's get in the cab.

658
00:30:11.880 --> 00:30:12.640
Get in the cab.

659
00:30:12.820 --> 00:30:13.460
You know what?

660
00:30:13.560 --> 00:30:14.300
How dare you?

661
00:30:14.480 --> 00:30:16.140
I'm like, OK, you've had enough.

662
00:30:16.380 --> 00:30:17.360
That was her tell.

663
00:30:17.920 --> 00:30:18.780
Yeah, that was her tell.

664
00:30:18.940 --> 00:30:19.540
How dare you?

665
00:30:19.880 --> 00:30:20.200
What?

666
00:30:20.320 --> 00:30:22.040
I just asked you to grab your purse.

667
00:30:22.040 --> 00:30:22.760
How dare you?

668
00:30:22.960 --> 00:30:23.720
OK, OK.

669
00:30:24.440 --> 00:30:29.940
I have to say another one of my favorite parts of this scene is the slow clap by Michael.

670
00:30:30.560 --> 00:30:34.200
He leads a slow clap as a way of defending Ryan.

671
00:30:34.640 --> 00:30:36.100
And I do love it.

672
00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:38.880
I thought it was a very bold choice by Michael.

673
00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:41.540
That's like an iconic movie moment.

674
00:30:41.760 --> 00:30:47.720
So, you know, I had to do a mini dive on the slow clap in movies because they are always

675
00:30:47.720 --> 00:30:48.500
amazing.

676
00:30:48.500 --> 00:30:52.080
They never, ever cease to not be amazing.

677
00:30:52.320 --> 00:30:58.200
When I went on IMDb and looked up how many movies had a slow clap, there's like a hundred.

678
00:30:58.580 --> 00:31:00.980
There's like so many movies.

679
00:31:01.240 --> 00:31:03.240
Jenna, sports movies have slow claps.

680
00:31:03.740 --> 00:31:06.640
Like law, dramatic movies have slow claps.

681
00:31:07.080 --> 00:31:09.500
Comedies have sarcastic slow claps.

682
00:31:09.500 --> 00:31:11.960
There are slow claps in every genre.

683
00:31:12.300 --> 00:31:16.560
I remember very clearly my introduction to the slow clap.

684
00:31:16.780 --> 00:31:20.600
I remember the first movie that I watched with a slow clap.

685
00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:24.880
Oh, lady, we all know the first movie we saw a slow clap in.

686
00:31:25.060 --> 00:31:26.460
I mean, what was yours?

687
00:31:27.040 --> 00:31:29.000
Can't Buy Me Love with Patrick Dempsey.

688
00:31:29.220 --> 00:31:31.580
Yes, absolutely.

689
00:31:32.360 --> 00:31:35.740
Famous slow clap at the tables outside.

690
00:31:36.200 --> 00:31:36.540
Mm-hmm.

691
00:31:36.940 --> 00:31:37.160
Yeah.

692
00:31:37.400 --> 00:31:37.940
Oh, yeah.

693
00:31:38.380 --> 00:31:44.180
So, first of all, I thought the slow clap was like an 80s, 90s movie thing because I remembered

694
00:31:44.180 --> 00:31:49.920
it from movies like Lucas, Cool Runnings, Officer and a Gentleman, Scent of a Woman, Rudy.

695
00:31:50.140 --> 00:31:50.860
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

696
00:31:50.940 --> 00:31:51.780
I have to stop you.

697
00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:56.840
There's a slow clap in Officer and a Gentleman and Scent of a Woman?

698
00:31:57.300 --> 00:31:57.740
Yes.

699
00:31:57.980 --> 00:31:58.760
Oh, Scent of a Woman.

