00:31:58.880 --> 00:32:00.240
It happens in the courtroom.

701
00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:00.740
No.

702
00:32:00.920 --> 00:32:03.080
Officer and a Gentleman, it happens in the factory.

703
00:32:03.480 --> 00:32:04.120
Yes.

704
00:32:04.320 --> 00:32:09.360
I'm sorry because it's shocking me because I really only associate the slow clap with

705
00:32:09.360 --> 00:32:10.820
80s teen movies.

706
00:32:11.140 --> 00:32:13.080
That's why I was freaking out.

707
00:32:13.320 --> 00:32:14.400
They're in dramas.

708
00:32:14.400 --> 00:32:17.880
They're everywhere, lady, especially in sports movies.

709
00:32:18.240 --> 00:32:18.380
Okay.

710
00:32:18.800 --> 00:32:24.400
Rudy, Hoosiers, Revenge of the Nerds, The Breakfast Club, Can't Buy Me Love, as you said,

711
00:32:24.860 --> 00:32:26.980
Not Another Teen Movie, Varsity Blues.

712
00:32:27.500 --> 00:32:28.640
Get ready for this one.

713
00:32:29.160 --> 00:32:29.940
Jersey Girl.

714
00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:30.920
Wow.

715
00:32:31.520 --> 00:32:33.040
Jersey Girl with Ben Affleck.

716
00:32:33.420 --> 00:32:36.400
Anyway, the list goes on and on, you guys.

717
00:32:36.560 --> 00:32:39.380
And I really thought it all started in the 80s and 90s.

718
00:32:39.500 --> 00:32:41.480
But according to the internet, I was wrong.

719
00:32:41.480 --> 00:32:50.720
The very first slow clap was in 1968 in a movie called The Lion in Winter, starring Peter O'Toole

720
00:32:50.720 --> 00:32:51.580
as Henry II.

721
00:32:51.680 --> 00:32:58.540
He slow claps to Catherine Hepburn as Eleanor of Aquitaine after her dramatic plea.

722
00:32:58.540 --> 00:32:59.580
Wow.

723
00:32:59.920 --> 00:33:00.660
I know.

724
00:33:00.960 --> 00:33:04.140
I feel like there are subcategories of slow claps.

725
00:33:04.400 --> 00:33:04.680
Mm-hmm.

726
00:33:04.680 --> 00:33:09.500
Ernest, sarcastic, joyous, rally the troops.

727
00:33:09.880 --> 00:33:12.040
Yes, inspirational slow clap.

728
00:33:12.260 --> 00:33:12.540
Mm-hmm.

729
00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:15.260
Angry, smart-ass slow clap.

730
00:33:15.260 --> 00:33:16.940
Thank you for doing that.

731
00:33:17.340 --> 00:33:17.780
You're welcome.

732
00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:20.160
Well, I found that fascinating, Angela.

733
00:33:20.160 --> 00:33:21.800
Moving on.

